// Title: Potential Iviewers.DLL Sideloading
// Sigma ID: 4c21b805-4dd7-469f-b47d-7383a8fcb437
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: X__Junior (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-03-21 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, execution, stealth, T1574.001
// Description: Detects potential DLL sideloading of "iviewers.dll" (OLE/COM Object Interface Viewer)
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.secureworks.com/research/shadowpad-malware-analysis
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_side_load_iviewers.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\iviewers.dll" and (not((FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Windows Kits\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files\\Windows Kits\\")))
